      "evidence": "The step says, for p>=2, “choose m with p<=2m and apply the same interpolation identity with 1/p between 1/2 and 1/(2m). Thus the stated two-sided estimate holds.” This interpolation gives the upper bound from the L2 and L2m bounds, but it does not give the lower bound. The omitted lower bound is the normalized-measure embedding ||f||_p >= ||f||_2=A, obtainable immediately from Hölder.",
